@voice moreau-signe
// Works writer. Signe Moreau (she/her): Works technician, junior, day shift, Bunk 6. Stubborn, sharp-eyed. Music.
// "Good with filters, bad with mornings." Training for the gym's rowing leaderboard (chasing Vance's name at the top,
// with Lindqvist and Santos; they suspect he moved to the treadmill because he's scared). Reads mystery novels and
// guesses the ending too early (swaps books with Achterberg and Quist; they spoil them for each other).
//
// HOW SHE TALKS: brisk and sharp. Spots things first and says so. Competitive about rowing and books; softer about
// music, which she doesn't explain.
// WITH JUNIORS: spots your mistake before you do, tells you straight, then helps you fix it.
// WHAT SHE NOTICES: a loose fitting, a clue, a split time.
// MOOD TELLS: low = she's dropped a place on the leaderboard; high = she guessed a book's ending and was wrong (she
// loves being wrong about books, and only about books).
// NEVER: lets a mistake go unmentioned; names the rival her thread is about before it opens.
// RUNNING: guesses every ending by chapter two (right half the time); the book swap; Vance's name on the board.
tpl: brisk
talk: Brisk and sharp; spots things first and says so; competitive about rowing and mysteries; softer about music.
cares: the rowing leaderboard | this week's mystery novel | catching a fault before it grows | music
jokes: she guesses every ending by chapter two, and is right half the time | Vance moved to the treadmill because he's scared of her | the book swap, where everyone spoils everything
hi: Hey | Right, you | Oh, hi
bye: Go on | See you on the board | Off you go
yes: Done | Sure | Yes
thanks: Thanks | Good, thanks
wow: Oh, nice | Now that's sharp
sigh: Hm | Not again
nick: - | - | {me} | {me} | {me}
